[{:db/id "8c445ad6-15c1-5fd2-8beb-f3aae92262ee" :answer/id #uuid "8c445ad6-15c1-5fd2-8beb-f3aae92262ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos{\\left(v \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(u + v \\right)}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e1265fd1-1562-50c9-b768-fc4b94890233" :answer/id #uuid "e1265fd1-1562-50c9-b768-fc4b94890233" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos{\\left(v \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(u - v \\right)}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "162cdffd-9949-51f0-8443-68942a4348a3" :answer/id #uuid "162cdffd-9949-51f0-8443-68942a4348a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos^{2}{\\left(u \\right)} \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b77893e6-ffd7-5547-9f92-80985949652f" :answer/id #uuid "b77893e6-ffd7-5547-9f92-80985949652f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3 \\cos{\\left(v \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(u + v \\right)}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5ec0dcc9-b1ef-5df4-b999-9593dcb919f9" :answer/id #uuid "5ec0dcc9-b1ef-5df4-b999-9593dcb919f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9 \\cos{\\left(v \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(u + v \\right)}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "88af74af-81f7-52da-9877-69b3c31c5d10" :answer-field/id #uuid "88af74af-81f7-52da-9877-69b3c31c5d10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["8c445ad6-15c1-5fd2-8beb-f3aae92262ee" "e1265fd1-1562-50c9-b768-fc4b94890233" "162cdffd-9949-51f0-8443-68942a4348a3" "b77893e6-ffd7-5547-9f92-80985949652f" "5ec0dcc9-b1ef-5df4-b999-9593dcb919f9"] :answer-field/correct "8c445ad6-15c1-5fd2-8beb-f3aae92262ee" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "ca197872-f947-536a-b45e-7bafb14c0796" :question/id #uuid "ca197872-f947-536a-b45e-7bafb14c0796" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $R$ in the $xyz$-space, given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z): 0\\le x + 3 y\\le \\frac{\\pi}{2},\\quad 0\\le - 3 y + z\\le \\frac{\\pi}{2},\\quad 0\\le z\\le 5\\}.\n$$\n\nGiven the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x + 3 y,\\quad v=- 3 y + z,\\quad w=z,\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be the missing part of the expression below?\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R 3 \\cos^{2}{\\left(x + z \\right)} \\cos{\\left(3 y - z \\right)}\\,dV=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{5}\\left(\\boxed{?}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:(u,v,w)\\longmapsto (x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w)).\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo find the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R f(x,y,z)\\,dV=\\iiint_Δ f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}\\right|\\,du\\,dv\\,dw\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x + 3 y,\\quad v=- 3 y + z,\\quad w=z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1}$.\n\n$$\nT^{-1}:(x,y,z)\\longmapsto (u(x,y,z),v(x,y,z),w(x,y,z)).\n$$\n\nTo find the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v,w): 0\\le u\\le \\frac{\\pi}{2},\\quad 0\\le v\\le \\frac{\\pi}{2},\\quad 0\\le w\\le 5\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z}\\\\\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z}\\\\\\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 & 0\\\\0 & -3 & 1\\\\0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\\\ &=(1)\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 1\\\\0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-(3)\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1\\\\0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+(0)\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3\\\\0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}\\\\ &=-3\\\\ &=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=- \\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R 3 \\cos^{2}{\\left(x + z \\right)} \\cos{\\left(3 y - z \\right)}\\,dV &=\\iiint_Δ \\left(3 \\cos{\\left(v \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(u + v \\right)}\\right)\\left|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\right|\\,du\\,dv\\,dw\\\\ &=\\iiint_Δ \\left(3 \\cos{\\left(v \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(u + v \\right)}\\right)\\left|- \\frac{1}{3}\\right|\\,du\\,dv\\,dw\\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{5}\\left(\\cos{\\left(v \\right)} \\cos^{2}{\\left(u + v \\right)}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["88af74af-81f7-52da-9877-69b3c31c5d10"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "ec8c848f-87b7-5107-8c5d-af33ba2dd461" :answer/id #uuid "ec8c848f-87b7-5107-8c5d-af33ba2dd461" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\sin{\\left(u \\right)} \\sin{\\left(v \\right)}}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "bf26d959-5bea-5cbd-b529-22a8c2a6d4d2" :answer/id #uuid "bf26d959-5bea-5cbd-b529-22a8c2a6d4d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3 \\sin{\\left(u \\right)} \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2b669794-92fe-524c-a98e-acbe50aa9636" :answer/id #uuid "2b669794-92fe-524c-a98e-acbe50aa9636" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6 \\sin{\\left(u \\right)} \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6e6bed85-1056-5bf5-82f0-56e822e9105d" :answer/id #uuid "6e6bed85-1056-5bf5-82f0-56e822e9105d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\sin{\\left(u \\right)} \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "75e67673-79a6-51f7-aea1-a3287b24b545" :answer/id #uuid "75e67673-79a6-51f7-aea1-a3287b24b545" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3 \\sin{\\left(v \\right)} \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ab6f2d4a-117f-5ba3-864f-ba275f597699" :answer-field/id #uuid "ab6f2d4a-117f-5ba3-864f-ba275f597699" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["ec8c848f-87b7-5107-8c5d-af33ba2dd461" "bf26d959-5bea-5cbd-b529-22a8c2a6d4d2" "2b669794-92fe-524c-a98e-acbe50aa9636" "6e6bed85-1056-5bf5-82f0-56e822e9105d" "75e67673-79a6-51f7-aea1-a3287b24b545"] :answer-field/correct "6e6bed85-1056-5bf5-82f0-56e822e9105d" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "f9a3dfe6-eaf9-53ba-8100-fedbe26e50f1" :question/id #uuid "f9a3dfe6-eaf9-53ba-8100-fedbe26e50f1" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $R$ in the $xyz$-space, given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z): \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}\\le 2 x + y\\le \\pi,\\quad 0\\le y + z\\le \\frac{\\pi}{2},\\quad -1\\le z\\le 5\\}.\n$$\n\nGiven the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=2 x + y,\\quad v=y + z,\\quad w=z,\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be the missing part of the expression below?\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R 3 \\sin{\\left(2 x + y \\right)} \\cos{\\left(y + z \\right)}\\,dV=\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{-1}^{5}\\left(\\boxed{?}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:(u,v,w)\\longmapsto (x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w)).\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo find the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R f(x,y,z)\\,dV=\\iiint_Δ f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}\\right|\\,du\\,dv\\,dw\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=2 x + y,\\quad v=y + z,\\quad w=z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1}$.\n\n$$\nT^{-1}:(x,y,z)\\longmapsto (u(x,y,z),v(x,y,z),w(x,y,z)).\n$$\n\nTo find the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v,w): \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}\\le u\\le \\pi,\\quad 0\\le v\\le \\frac{\\pi}{2},\\quad -1\\le w\\le 5\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z}\\\\\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z}\\\\\\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 & 0\\\\0 & 1 & 1\\\\0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}\\\\ &=(2)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1\\\\0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-(1)\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1\\\\0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+(0)\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1\\\\0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}\\\\ &=2\\\\ &=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R 3 \\sin{\\left(2 x + y \\right)} \\cos{\\left(y + z \\right)}\\,dV &=\\iiint_Δ \\left(3 \\sin{\\left(u \\right)} \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}\\right)\\left|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\right|\\,du\\,dv\\,dw\\\\ &=\\iiint_Δ \\left(3 \\sin{\\left(u \\right)} \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}\\right)\\left|\\frac{1}{2}\\right|\\,du\\,dv\\,dw\\\\ &=\\int_{\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{-1}^{5}\\left(\\frac{3 \\sin{\\left(u \\right)} \\cos{\\left(v \\right)}}{2}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["ab6f2d4a-117f-5ba3-864f-ba275f597699"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "55eff19e-64a0-58c9-a3ac-3a4127bd2f3a" :answer/id #uuid "55eff19e-64a0-58c9-a3ac-3a4127bd2f3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{\\sqrt{u v}}\\left(3 w^{2}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b82588e5-cfb7-5f6d-81d3-92f9dedf9c10" :answer/id #uuid "b82588e5-cfb7-5f6d-81d3-92f9dedf9c10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{\\sqrt{u + v}}\\left(3 w^{2}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2b3df91c-acac-5c15-a4be-f4c02430118e" :answer/id #uuid "2b3df91c-acac-5c15-a4be-f4c02430118e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{\\sqrt{u v}}\\left(\\frac{3 w}{2}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "3d6a0298-2596-572e-b463-351496792e13" :answer/id #uuid "3d6a0298-2596-572e-b463-351496792e13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{\\sqrt{u v}}\\left(3 w\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6f82d57c-839e-59bf-be77-b81ccfd2d25a" :answer/id #uuid "6f82d57c-839e-59bf-be77-b81ccfd2d25a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{u v}\\left(3 w^{2}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d3257502-4734-5a4a-a6fe-1b87f74cb8aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "d3257502-4734-5a4a-a6fe-1b87f74cb8aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["55eff19e-64a0-58c9-a3ac-3a4127bd2f3a" "b82588e5-cfb7-5f6d-81d3-92f9dedf9c10" "2b3df91c-acac-5c15-a4be-f4c02430118e" "3d6a0298-2596-572e-b463-351496792e13" "6f82d57c-839e-59bf-be77-b81ccfd2d25a"] :answer-field/correct "55eff19e-64a0-58c9-a3ac-3a4127bd2f3a" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "a02015c9-3dc8-5d87-84de-d3d182e3bfdc" :question/id #uuid "a02015c9-3dc8-5d87-84de-d3d182e3bfdc" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $R$ in the $xyz$-space, given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z): 1\\le x + y\\le 3,\\quad 1\\le x - y\\le 3,\\quad 1\\le z\\le \\left(x - y\\right) \\left(x + y\\right)\\}.\n$$\n\nGiven the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x + y,\\quad v=x - y,\\quad w=\\sqrt{z},\n$$\n\nWrite the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R 3 \\sqrt{z}\\,dV\n$$\n\nas a repeated integral in terms of $u$, $v$, and $w$." :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:(u,v,w)\\longmapsto (x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w)).\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo find the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R f(x,y,z)\\,dV=\\iiint_Δ f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}\\right|\\,du\\,dv\\,dw\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x + y,\\quad v=x - y,\\quad w=\\sqrt{z}\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1}$.\n\n$$\nT^{-1}:(x,y,z)\\longmapsto (u(x,y,z),v(x,y,z),w(x,y,z)).\n$$\n\nTo find the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v,w): 1\\le u\\le 3,\\quad 1\\le v\\le 3,\\quad 1\\le w\\le \\sqrt{u v}\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z}\\\\\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z}\\\\\\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 & 0\\\\1 & -1 & 0\\\\0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{z}}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\ &=(1)\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0\\\\0 & \\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{z}}\\end{vmatrix}-(1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0\\\\0 & \\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{z}}\\end{vmatrix}+(0)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1\\\\0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}\\\\ &=- \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{z}}\\\\ &=- \\frac{1}{w}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=- w.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$ Since $z\\ge1$ and $w=\\sqrt z$, the branch is $w>0$.\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R 3 \\sqrt{z}\\,dV &=\\iiint_Δ \\left(3 w\\right)\\left|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\right|\\,du\\,dv\\,dw\\\\ &=\\iiint_Δ \\left(3 w\\right)\\left|- w\\right|\\,du\\,dv\\,dw\\\\ &=\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{3}\\int_{1}^{\\sqrt{u v}}\\left(3 w^{2}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["d3257502-4734-5a4a-a6fe-1b87f74cb8aa"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "026d0fdb-c581-5805-a7ce-956120cb2488" :answer/id #uuid "026d0fdb-c581-5805-a7ce-956120cb2488" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{-2}^{-1}\\int_{0}^{8}\\left(\\frac{- 12 u - v w}{16 v}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "834210eb-ce4e-561d-8caa-3539a509f6f5" :answer/id #uuid "834210eb-ce4e-561d-8caa-3539a509f6f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{-2}^{-1}\\int_{0}^{8}\\left(\\frac{v \\left(12 u + w\\right)}{4}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a09b199f-4fbe-567e-bbbf-f1eda74093e1" :answer/id #uuid "a09b199f-4fbe-567e-bbbf-f1eda74093e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{-2}^{-1}\\int_{0}^{8}\\left(v^{2} \\left(- 12 u - w\\right)\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7b55cdc3-8c0c-5ff2-b9be-cfd98c564cda" :answer/id #uuid "7b55cdc3-8c0c-5ff2-b9be-cfd98c564cda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{-2}^{-1}\\int_{0}^{8}\\left(- \\frac{3 u}{4} - \\frac{w}{16}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1d254e30-5cb5-5b46-93cb-81d3d3153a4e" :answer/id #uuid "1d254e30-5cb5-5b46-93cb-81d3d3153a4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{-2}^{-1}\\int_{0}^{8}\\left(- \\frac{3 u}{4} - \\frac{w}{4}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2b93097b-db4a-5d04-a26f-2558e108a845" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b93097b-db4a-5d04-a26f-2558e108a845" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["026d0fdb-c581-5805-a7ce-956120cb2488" "834210eb-ce4e-561d-8caa-3539a509f6f5" "a09b199f-4fbe-567e-bbbf-f1eda74093e1" "7b55cdc3-8c0c-5ff2-b9be-cfd98c564cda" "1d254e30-5cb5-5b46-93cb-81d3d3153a4e"] :answer-field/correct "7b55cdc3-8c0c-5ff2-b9be-cfd98c564cda" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "5a980a84-b104-5f71-8ad4-d675189b5a6a" :question/id #uuid "5a980a84-b104-5f71-8ad4-d675189b5a6a" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $R$ in the $xyz$-space, given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z): 1\\le x y\\le 2,\\quad -2\\le y\\le -1,\\quad 0\\le z\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nGiven the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x y,\\quad v=y,\\quad w=4 z,\n$$\n\nWrite the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R 3 x y^{2} + y z\\,dV\n$$\n\nas a repeated integral in terms of $u$, $v$, and $w$." :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:(u,v,w)\\longmapsto (x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w)).\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo find the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R f(x,y,z)\\,dV=\\iiint_Δ f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}\\right|\\,du\\,dv\\,dw\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x y,\\quad v=y,\\quad w=4 z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1}$.\n\n$$\nT^{-1}:(x,y,z)\\longmapsto (u(x,y,z),v(x,y,z),w(x,y,z)).\n$$\n\nTo find the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v,w): 1\\le u\\le 2,\\quad -2\\le v\\le -1,\\quad 0\\le w\\le 8\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z}\\\\\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z}\\\\\\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{vmatrix}y & x & 0\\\\0 & 1 & 0\\\\0 & 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\\\\ &=(y)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0\\\\0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}-(x)\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0\\\\0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}+(0)\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1\\\\0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}\\\\ &=4 y\\\\ &=4 v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{4 v}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$ The sign of $v$ is fixed throughout $Δ$.\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R 3 x y^{2} + y z\\,dV &=\\iiint_Δ \\left(\\frac{v \\left(12 u + w\\right)}{4}\\right)\\left|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\right|\\,du\\,dv\\,dw\\\\ &=\\iiint_Δ \\left(\\frac{v \\left(12 u + w\\right)}{4}\\right)\\left|\\frac{1}{4 v}\\right|\\,du\\,dv\\,dw\\\\ &=\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{-2}^{-1}\\int_{0}^{8}\\left(- \\frac{3 u}{4} - \\frac{w}{16}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["2b93097b-db4a-5d04-a26f-2558e108a845"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "384ceb69-cecb-55f9-aed6-e3bd5b768cf5" :answer/id #uuid "384ceb69-cecb-55f9-aed6-e3bd5b768cf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{0}^{12}\\left(\\frac{u}{2} + \\frac{3 w}{4}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "60dff23d-d505-50f8-a62e-061ce9cf5786" :answer/id #uuid "60dff23d-d505-50f8-a62e-061ce9cf5786" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{0}^{12}\\left(v^{2} \\left(8 u + 3 w\\right)\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f2a8a28d-7150-565f-9912-f59fafb22f59" :answer/id #uuid "f2a8a28d-7150-565f-9912-f59fafb22f59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{0}^{12}\\left(\\frac{u}{2 v} + \\frac{3 w}{16}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "3f0c525f-3134-5b92-ab7a-9e88bd710485" :answer/id #uuid "3f0c525f-3134-5b92-ab7a-9e88bd710485" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{0}^{12}\\left(\\frac{v \\left(8 u + 3 w\\right)}{4}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "092324b9-324a-577d-8187-0a5286f7ef1b" :answer/id #uuid "092324b9-324a-577d-8187-0a5286f7ef1b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{0}^{12}\\left(\\frac{u}{2} + \\frac{3 w}{16}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2cb431a1-e3de-516b-9ca4-9afe0bfddacf" :answer-field/id #uuid "2cb431a1-e3de-516b-9ca4-9afe0bfddacf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["384ceb69-cecb-55f9-aed6-e3bd5b768cf5" "60dff23d-d505-50f8-a62e-061ce9cf5786" "f2a8a28d-7150-565f-9912-f59fafb22f59" "3f0c525f-3134-5b92-ab7a-9e88bd710485" "092324b9-324a-577d-8187-0a5286f7ef1b"] :answer-field/correct "092324b9-324a-577d-8187-0a5286f7ef1b" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "cdc4fd63-3878-558d-af8d-65bb9f7d74a4" :question/id #uuid "cdc4fd63-3878-558d-af8d-65bb9f7d74a4" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $R$ in the $xyz$-space, given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z): 1\\le x y\\le 2,\\quad 1\\le y\\le 2,\\quad 0\\le z\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nGiven the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x y,\\quad v=y,\\quad w=4 z,\n$$\n\nWrite the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R 2 x y^{2} + 3 y z\\,dV\n$$\n\nas a repeated integral in terms of $u$, $v$, and $w$." :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:(u,v,w)\\longmapsto (x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w)).\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo find the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R f(x,y,z)\\,dV=\\iiint_Δ f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}\\right|\\,du\\,dv\\,dw\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x y,\\quad v=y,\\quad w=4 z\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1}$.\n\n$$\nT^{-1}:(x,y,z)\\longmapsto (u(x,y,z),v(x,y,z),w(x,y,z)).\n$$\n\nTo find the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v,w): 1\\le u\\le 2,\\quad 1\\le v\\le 2,\\quad 0\\le w\\le 12\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z}\\\\\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z}\\\\\\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{vmatrix}y & x & 0\\\\0 & 1 & 0\\\\0 & 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}\\\\ &=(y)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0\\\\0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}-(x)\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0\\\\0 & 4\\end{vmatrix}+(0)\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1\\\\0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}\\\\ &=4 y\\\\ &=4 v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{4 v}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$ The sign of $v$ is fixed throughout $Δ$.\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R 2 x y^{2} + 3 y z\\,dV &=\\iiint_Δ \\left(\\frac{v \\left(8 u + 3 w\\right)}{4}\\right)\\left|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\right|\\,du\\,dv\\,dw\\\\ &=\\iiint_Δ \\left(\\frac{v \\left(8 u + 3 w\\right)}{4}\\right)\\left|\\frac{1}{4 v}\\right|\\,du\\,dv\\,dw\\\\ &=\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{1}^{2}\\int_{0}^{12}\\left(\\frac{u}{2} + \\frac{3 w}{16}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["2cb431a1-e3de-516b-9ca4-9afe0bfddacf"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "c66fca7b-36c4-56cb-8c0c-ac1faa865c3c" :answer/id #uuid "c66fca7b-36c4-56cb-8c0c-ac1faa865c3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{4}\\int_{1}^{4}\\int_{1}^{\\sqrt{u v}}\\left(4 w^{2}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "01570206-5cdd-5e6b-9104-73e9fcfb4d9d" :answer/id #uuid "01570206-5cdd-5e6b-9104-73e9fcfb4d9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{4}\\int_{1}^{4}\\int_{1}^{u v}\\left(4 w^{2}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b540dafe-8822-5831-96de-99fe23d46ba5" :answer/id #uuid "b540dafe-8822-5831-96de-99fe23d46ba5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{4}\\int_{1}^{4}\\int_{1}^{\\sqrt{u v}}\\left(2 w\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "3f8ad14c-de95-56d5-905f-adc4c1595467" :answer/id #uuid "3f8ad14c-de95-56d5-905f-adc4c1595467" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{4}\\int_{1}^{4}\\int_{1}^{\\sqrt{u v}}\\left(4 w\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7208a6f8-db4c-57ff-b758-167c5cbcf08c" :answer/id #uuid "7208a6f8-db4c-57ff-b758-167c5cbcf08c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{1}^{4}\\int_{1}^{4}\\int_{1}^{\\sqrt{u + v}}\\left(4 w^{2}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4bae0846-9e7d-581b-a860-26c008b5e751" :answer-field/id #uuid "4bae0846-9e7d-581b-a860-26c008b5e751" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["c66fca7b-36c4-56cb-8c0c-ac1faa865c3c" "01570206-5cdd-5e6b-9104-73e9fcfb4d9d" "b540dafe-8822-5831-96de-99fe23d46ba5" "3f8ad14c-de95-56d5-905f-adc4c1595467" "7208a6f8-db4c-57ff-b758-167c5cbcf08c"] :answer-field/correct "c66fca7b-36c4-56cb-8c0c-ac1faa865c3c" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "2b76035f-4083-5963-886f-519463991382" :question/id #uuid "2b76035f-4083-5963-886f-519463991382" :question/problem "Consider the finite region $R$ in the $xyz$-space, given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z): 1\\le x + y\\le 4,\\quad 1\\le x - y\\le 4,\\quad 1\\le z\\le \\left(x - y\\right) \\left(x + y\\right)\\}.\n$$\n\nGiven the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x + y,\\quad v=x - y,\\quad w=\\sqrt{z},\n$$\n\nWrite the triple integral\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R 4 \\sqrt{z}\\,dV\n$$\n\nas a repeated integral in terms of $u$, $v$, and $w$." :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:(u,v,w)\\longmapsto (x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w)).\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uvw$-space to our region $R$ in the $xyz$-space.\n\nTo find the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n\\iiint_R f(x,y,z)\\,dV=\\iiint_Δ f(x(u,v,w),y(u,v,w),z(u,v,w))\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y,z)}{\\partial(u,v,w)}\\right|\\,du\\,dv\\,dw\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nNote that the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x + y,\\quad v=x - y,\\quad w=\\sqrt{z}\n$$\n\ngives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1}$.\n\n$$\nT^{-1}:(x,y,z)\\longmapsto (u(x,y,z),v(x,y,z),w(x,y,z)).\n$$\n\nTo find the required integral, we proceed in four steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $R$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nOur domain in the $uvw$-space is\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v,w): 1\\le u\\le 4,\\quad 1\\le v\\le 4,\\quad 1\\le w\\le \\sqrt{u v}\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)} &=\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial z}\\\\\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial z}\\\\\\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial w}{\\partial z}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\ &=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 & 0\\\\1 & -1 & 0\\\\0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{z}}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\ &=(1)\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0\\\\0 & \\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{z}}\\end{vmatrix}-(1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0\\\\0 & \\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{z}}\\end{vmatrix}+(0)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1\\\\0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}\\\\ &=- \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{z}}\\\\ &=- \\frac{1}{w}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=\\left(\\frac{∂(u,v,w)}{∂(x,y,z)}\\right)^{-1}=- w.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$ Since $z\\ge1$ and $w=\\sqrt z$, the branch is $w>0$.\n\n**Step 4**: Perform the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iiint_R 4 \\sqrt{z}\\,dV &=\\iiint_Δ \\left(4 w\\right)\\left|\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}\\right|\\,du\\,dv\\,dw\\\\ &=\\iiint_Δ \\left(4 w\\right)\\left|- w\\right|\\,du\\,dv\\,dw\\\\ &=\\int_{1}^{4}\\int_{1}^{4}\\int_{1}^{\\sqrt{u v}}\\left(4 w^{2}\\right)\\,dw\\,dv\\,du.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["4bae0846-9e7d-581b-a860-26c008b5e751"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "bf472042-3f5c-5281-ade2-20799b3f9ef5" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186198397.py"} [:db/add 17592186198397 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] {:db/id 17592186198397 :knowledge-point/questions ["ca197872-f947-536a-b45e-7bafb14c0796" "f9a3dfe6-eaf9-53ba-8100-fedbe26e50f1" "a02015c9-3dc8-5d87-84de-d3d182e3bfdc" "5a980a84-b104-5f71-8ad4-d675189b5a6a" "cdc4fd63-3878-558d-af8d-65bb9f7d74a4" "2b76035f-4083-5963-886f-519463991382"]} [:db/ensure 17592186198397 :knowledge-point/validate]]
